{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_42","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Program Files\\\\PowerShell\\\\7\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command '$r=toml?; $lines=Get-Content docs/test/test-cases.toml; $i=($lines|Select-String '\"'\"'^'\"\\\\[test.TC-278\\\\]\"'$'\"').LineNumber; \"'$lines[($i-1)..($i+10)]; $l=Get-Content docs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml; $j=($l|Select-String '\"'\"'^'\"\\\\[design.LLR-278\\\\]\"'$'\"').LineNumber; \"'$l[($j-1)..($j+10)]'","aggregated_output":"toml?: \r\nLine |\r\n   2 |  $r=toml?; $lines=Get-Content docs/test/test-cases.toml; $i=($lines|Se …\r\n     |     ~~~~~\r\n     | The term 'toml?' is not recognized as a name of a cmdlet, function, script file, or executable program.\r\nCheck the spelling of the name, or if a path was included, verify that the path is correct and try again.\r\n[test.TC-278]\r\nverifies = [\"SR-178\", \"SR-208\", \"SR-228\", \"LLR-278\", \"IF-091\", \"LLR-246\"]\r\nlevel = \"Integration\"\r\nmethod = \"Driven on real git repositories made from scaffolds. An adjudication lane claiming an amendment row scoped to one requirement, whose act re-attests two amended requirements, is refused at merge naming the one outside the scope; an act re-attesting only the scoped row merges, and the same act claimed by a first-approval row is refused naming the row, since that lane holds no re-attestation scope. A combined act across the same or different registries merges when each section acts only within its own kind scope and every copied registry has an acted row, including a ledger-only approval; a copied registry neither section moved is WIDENED. On a RELEASED rung, an act naming an unaccepted verdict is refused by the verdict named, and its whole act, a first approval included, is refused. Each act permitted to merge in these cases carries branch bindings that judge every row it flips APPROVE and every row it re-attests CLARITY, or MEANING with the bless mark, written by _bind_branch; a named verdict must itself be accepted and authorize each row its act re-attests in the same way, and omitting --verdict does not waive the branch binding. On a RELEASED rung, an act re-attesting a row that its accepted amendment verdict rules plain MEANING, or tags MEANING+BLESS and another way, is refused naming the row, through the backing check and through a named verdict alike. A combined act carrying one is refused whole. The same act under a MEANING+BLESS ruling merges. A first-approval part that RETURNs its only judged row approves nothing, while its combined act may re-attest its amendment row. One act that approves a Drafted requirement and re-attests an amended one, claimed by a first-approval row scoped to the first and an amendment row scoped to the second, merges; the same act whose amendment row is scoped to another requirement is refused naming the re-attested row. On a RELEASED rung, an act whose only re-attestation retires an Approved row the lane deleted, ruled by an accepted amendment verdict inside the amendment scope, merges with that registry's copy as its only copy. The same retirement on a held rung is refused by row. The amendment brief renders one judged-text digest per shown row, reservation writes those identities in the binding, accepted and failed outcome rewrites preserve them, and the act turn refuses before launching an adjudicator when held text moved.\"\r\ntier = \"Full\"\r\nexpected = \"Satisfies LLR-278 (parents SR-178 and SR-228): a re-attestation outside the amendment row's Adjudicates scope is refused at merge by name; every acted approval, including a ledger-only approval, needs its approved rows APPROVE-ruled and its re-attested rows CLARITY-ruled, or MEANING-ruled with the bless mark, by accepted branch bindings, and a named verdict authorizes each row it re-attests in the same way; and an act whose approvals and re-attestations each lie in the scope of the row claiming them merges. A retired row's re-attestation authorizes its own registry's copy, whether or not another act moved that registry. A held CLARITY re-attestation is actable only when the accepted binding's identity equals the committed row's approved-text digest; an absent, malformed or unequal identity yields a row-naming refusal before launch.\"\r\nautomated = \"Yes\"\r\nevidence = \"tests/test_snapshot_readers.py::test_a_reattestation_outside_the_amendment_scope_is_refused_by_name; tests/test_snapshot_readers.py::test_a_reattestation_inside_the_amendment_scope_merges; tests/test_snapshot_readers.py::test_a_held_rung_reattestation_without_a_verdict_is_refused; tests/test_snapshot_readers.py::test_a_held_rung_reattestation_its_verdict_rules_CLARITY_merges; tests/test_snapshot_readers.py::test_a_held_rung_reattestation_of_a_MEANING_row_is_refused; tests/test_snapshot_readers.py::test_a_held_rung_is_read_from_trunk_not_from_the_merge_base; tests/test_snapshot_readers.py::test_a_held_rung_reattestation_of_a_DRAFTED_row_is_refused; tests/test_snapshot_readers.py::test_a_held_rung_reattestation_its_verdict_does_not_rule_is_refused; tests/test_snapshot_readers.py::test_a_held_rung_reattestation_whose_verdict_is_unreadable_is_refused; tests/test_snapshot_readers.py::test_a_held_rung_row_ruled_both_ways_reads_MEANING_and_is_refused; tests/test_snapshot_readers.py::test_a_mixed_approval_and_reattestation_act_merges; tests/test_snapshot_readers.py::test_a_mixed_act_reattesting_outside_its_amendment_scope_is_refused; tests/test_snapshot_readers.py::test_a_combined_sittings_sections_each_take_their_own_act; tests/test_snapshot_readers.py::test_a_combined_sittings_act_outside_its_kinds_tokens_is_refused; tests/test_snapshot_readers.py::test_a_combined_act_in_two_registries_merges; tests/test_snapshot_readers.py::test_a_combined_act_whose_first_approval_returned_everything_merges; tests/test_snapshot_readers.py::test_a_combined_act_copying_a_registry_neither_section_moved_is_widened; tests/test_snapshot_readers.py::test_a_combined_act_on_a_csv_carrier_authorizes_the_copy_it_writes; tests/test_snapshot_readers.py::test_a_combined_act_on_a_markdown_needs_carrier_authorizes_its_copy; tests/test_snapshot_readers.py::test_a_combined_act_across_a_needs_carrier_conversion_merges; tests/test_snapshot_readers.py::test_a_plain_flip_across_a_needs_carrier_conversion_merges; tests/test_snapshot_readers.py::test_an_unauthorized_registrys_obsolete_copy_is_still_widened; tests/test_snapshot_readers.py::test_a_rejected_bound_sitting_cannot_carry_a_held_rung_reattestation; tests/test_snapshot_readers.py::test_a_released_tier_act_naming_an_unaccepted_verdict_is_refused; tests/test_snapshot_readers.py::test_a_first_approval_in_an_act_naming_an_unaccepted_verdict_is_refused; tests/test_snapshot_readers.py::test_an_act_omitting_its_verdict_is_still_tied_to_an_accepted_one; tests/test_snapshot_readers.py::test_an_accepted_sitting_over_other_rows_does_not_authorize_this_act; tests/test_snapshot_readers.py::test_a_single_kind_verdict_over_other_rows_does_not_authorize; tests/test_snapshot_readers.py::test_a_named_verdict_must_judge_the_rows_it_reattests; tests/test_snapshot_readers.py::test_a_single_kind_first_approval_of_its_judged_row_merges; tests/test_integrate_admission.py::test_a_ledger_only_approval_outside_the_scope_is_refused; tests/test_integrate_admission.py::test_a_backed_ledger_only_approval_on_an_ordinary_lane_is_admitted; tests/test_integrate_admission.py::test_an_unbacked_ledger_only_approval_is_refused_by_name; tests/test_snapshot_readers.py::test_a_retirement_alone_in_its_registry_merges; tests/test_snapshot_readers.py::test_the_acted_set_names_a_retired_rows_registry; tests/test_snapshot_readers.py::test_a_lone_retirement_on_a_held_rung_is_refused_by_row; tests/test_snapshot_readers.py::test_a_retirement_outside_the_amendment_scope_is_refused; tests/test_snapshot_readers.py::test_a_retirement_no_accepted_verdict_rules_is_refused; tests/test_snapshot_readers.py::test_a_retirement_beside_another_act_in_its_registry_merges; tests/test_snapshot_readers.py::test_a_released_plain_MEANING_reattestation_is_refused_naming_the_row_and_the_mark; tests/test_snapshot_readers.py::test_a_released_MEANING_BLESS_reattestation_merges; tests/test_snapshot_readers.py::test_a_released_row_tagged_two_ways_is_refused; tests/test_snapshot_readers.py::test_a_named_verdict_ruling_the_row_plain_MEANING_is_refused_naming_the_verdict; tests/test_snapshot_readers.py::test_a_named_verdict_blessing_the_row_merges; tests/test_snapshot_readers.py::test_a_combined_act_carrying_a_plain_MEANING_reattestation_is_refused_whole; tests/test_snapshot_readers.py::test_a_combined_act_with_a_blessed_reattestation_merges; tests/test_adjudicate_brief.py::test_the_amendment_brief_states_each_shown_rows_digest; tests/test_adjudicate_brief.py::test_bind_pending_records_the_briefs_identities; tests/test_adjudicate_brief.py::test_record_outcome_keeps_the_identity_cell; tests/test_adjudicate_act.py::test_a_held_CLARITY_act_bound_to_the_exact_text_is_owed; tests/test_adjudicate_act.py::test_a_held_CLARITY_act_whose_text_changed_after_the_verdict_is_refused; tests/test_adjudicate_act.py::test_a_held_CLARITY_act_whose_binding_has_no_identity_is_refused; tests/test_coordinator_act.py::test_the_act_turn_refuses_before_launch_when_held_text_moved; tests/test_held_status_git.py::test_a_held_CLARITY_reattestation_bound_to_the_exact_text_lands; tests/test_held_status_git.py::test_held_text_changed_after_its_CLARITY_verdict_is_refused_at_the_slot; tests/test_held_status_git.py::test_a_binding_with_no_identity_cell_is_refused; tests/test_held_status_git.py::test_a_held_MEANING_BLESS_reattestation_is_refused\"\r\nstatus = \"Approved\"\r\nphase = 6\r\n\r\n[test.TC-279]\r\n[design.LLR-278]\r\nsr_refs = [\"SR-178\", \"SR-228\"]\r\ntitle = \"An adjudication re-attestation constrained at merge\"\r\nmodule = \"project-trajectory/scripts/acceptance_record.py;project-trajectory/scripts/kitlib/verdict.py\"\r\ncode_symbol = \"first_approval_scope/adjudication_approval_refusal/merge_approval_refusal/_registry_identity/lane_acted_set/_copy_lines/amendment_scope/reattested_between/_wrote_ledger/_added_acts/row_rulings/verdict_rulings/_tier_of/_below_approval/_held_row_line/_held_act_lines/held_reattest_refusal/reattest_scope_refusal\"\r\ndetail = \"acceptance_record.merge_approval_refusal applies the additional adjudication bounds whenever any claimed row records a scope, including a mixed lane, and calls reattest_scope_refusal for that scope-bound lane. A malformed combined token is refused by name; an act-free delta has no scope refusal. reattested_between reads the ledger at the merge base and the head and takes the ids re-attested by the entries whose seq the base does not hold, refusing by name when either side does not parse. Every such id outside amendment_scope - the union of the claimed amendment rows' own amendment scope, including their amendment:<id> tokens when a combined sitting claims them, empty when none is claimed - is refused by name before the first-approval judgement runs. Every approval act in the lane’s complete acted set - a live flip or born-approved row, a ledger-only approval, or a re-attestation - is refused when any row it approves lacks an APPROVE ruling in an accepted first-approval part or any row it re-attests lacks a CLARITY ruling, or a MEANING ruling carrying the bless mark, in an accepted amendment part among the branch's bindings, whether or not the act names a verdict; a named verdict must also authorize every row its act re-attests in the same way, and acts already on trunk are not re-read. An act that both approves rows and re-attests rows, claimed either by two single-kind rows or by one combined sitting's per-kind tokens, merges when each half lies inside its claiming row's own kind scope, whether their rows are in one registry or different ones; an id under another combined kind authorizes neither half, a snapshot is WIDENED only when the complete acted set holds no approved or re-attested row in that registry identity, a row the act ledger names being placed in the registry its id's tier names whether or not the row remains in the live registry at the head, so a retirement authorizes its own registry's copy: every carrier path of an authorized registry, including a deleted obsolete carrier copy, is authorized, while an unauthorized registry's copy is WIDENED on every carrier path.\"\r\ntest_refs = \"TC-278; TC-331; tests/test_adjudicate_brief.py::test_the_amendment_brief_states_each_shown_rows_digest; tests/test_adjudicate_brief.py::test_bind_pending_records_the_briefs_identities; tests/test_adjudicate_brief.py::test_record_outcome_keeps_the_identity_cell; tests/test_adjudicate_act.py::test_a_held_CLARITY_act_whose_text_changed_after_the_verdict_is_refused; tests/test_coordinator_act.py::test_the_act_turn_refuses_before_launch_when_held_text_moved\"\r\nrationale = \"\"\"At merge the first-approval scope check read flips alone, and a re-attestation moves no cell, so an amendment act could re-anchor rows its verdict never ruled. The act ledger is the one record naming the rows each act re-attested, which makes the scope checkable where the merge is judged; a scope-bound lane claiming no amendment has ruled no amended text, so it may re-anchor none.\"\"\"\r\nstatus = \"Approved\"\r\ncomponent = \"CMP-006\"\r\nphase = 6\r\n\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
